HarmonyOS PC (HMDFS) portability: relax the temporary-directory umask in
configure from 077 to 022.

The HMDFS filesystem forces the setgid bit on newly created directories.
Creating the ./confstatXXXXXX scratch directory under `umask 077` therefore
yields drwx--S--- instead of drwx--x---, which blocks even the owning process
from writing into it. config.status then fails while assembling its
substitution files:

    ./config.status: line 444: ./confstatXXXXXX/subs.sed: Permission denied
    ./config.status: line 526: ./confstatXXXXXX/subs.frag: Permission denied
    ./config.status: line 697: ./confstatXXXXXX/out: Permission denied
    mv: bad './confstatXXXXXX/out': Permission denied
    config.status: executing depfiles commands

and no Makefile is produced, so the following make run aborts because there is
no makefile for it to read.

Using 022 keeps the directory owner-writable, which is what config.status needs
to write its scratch files. The directory is still created inside the build tree
and removed by configure's existing trap, so nothing is left readable outside
the build directory.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -3416,12 +3416,12 @@
 # Create a (secure) tmp directory for tmp files.

 {
-  tmp=`(umask 077 && mktemp -d -q "./confstatXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
+  tmp=`(umask 022 && mktemp -d -q "./confstatXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
   test -n "$tmp" && test -d "$tmp"
 }  ||
 {
   tmp=./confstat$$-$RANDOM
-  (umask 077 && mkdir $tmp)
+  (umask 022 && mkdir $tmp)
 } ||
 {
    echo "$me: cannot create a temporary directory in ." >&2
